/*!
\page page_sttrackdetectorinfo StTrackDetectorInfo

\brief Hit references and per-detector hit-count summaries for a reconstructed track.

\section sttrackdetectorinfo_overview Overview

\ref StTrackDetectorInfo is shared between an \c StGlobalTrack and its sibling
\c StPrimaryTrack objects.  It stores:
- Non-owning pointers to all \c StHit objects associated with the track.
- Per-detector counts of measured hits.
- Global positions of the innermost and outermost hits.

\section sttrackdetectorinfo_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackDetectorInfo
\endcode

\section sttrackdetectorinfo_members Data Members

| Member | Description |
|---|---|
| \c mFirstPoint | Global position of the innermost hit (cm). |
| \c mLastPoint | Global position of the outermost hit (cm). |
| \c mNumberOfPointsTpc | TPC hit count (ITTF encoding). |
| \c mNumberOfPointsFtpcWest | FTPC west hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsFtpcEast | FTPC east hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsSvt | SVT hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsSsd | SSD/SST hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsOth | Other-detector hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsIst | IST hit count. |
| \c mNumberOfPointsPxl | PXL hit count. |
| \c mHits | \c StPtrVecHit — all associated hit pointers. |

\section sttrackdetectorinfo_ittf ITTF Encoding Note

When \c mNumberOfPoints == 0, the individual per-detector members are authoritative.
When \c mNumberOfPoints != 0, legacy packed encoding (TPC%1000 + SVT/1000%10 + SSD/10000)
is active.  Both are decoded transparently by \c numberOfPoints(StDetectorId).

\section sttrackdetectorinfo_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StTrackDetectorInfo* info = track->detectorInfo();
unsigned short nTpc = info->numberOfPoints(kTpcId);
StPtrVecHit tpcHits = info->hits(kTpcId);
for (StHit* hit : tpcHits) { /* process hit */ }
\endcode

\see StTrack
\see StHit
*/
